    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d159">

                <pb facs="0149" n="139" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg139"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/10–2149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Holmes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-10-21T19:00:00+01:00">October 21, 1949—7
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 21—2:16 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4235. Embtel 4173, October 18. In further conversation with Dening this afternoon
                    he stated emphatically that Bevin–Acheson understanding reached in Washington
                    would include consultation in <pb facs="0150" n="140" xml:id="pg140"/> advance
                    regarding <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> as well <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >de jure</hi> recognition Chinese Communists. Memorandum of conversation by
                        air.<anchor n="43" xml:id="d159-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Holmes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
